	### Feature Workspace Bootstrap
	Before starting the analysis:
	If Documentation/SDD/<feature-slug>/ does not exist:
	- Create the standard feature workspace structure.
	- Initialize the standard SDD documents according to project conventions.
	- Register the feature in Documentation/State.md as Research Phase, preserving approved project sequencing.
	- Continue with Research Part 1.
	If the workspace already exists:
	- Continue from existing artifacts.
	- Preserve previously approved documentation and decisions.
	- Do not overwrite existing content unless explicitly requested.
	### Session Rules (Mandatory)
	- Do NOT implement code.
	- Do NOT modify production files, tests, migrations, or configuration.
	- Do NOT update owning documentation ( State.md, PM, PRD, ADRs, architecture/technical docs, rules, skills). Identify update candidates only, except for the Feature Workspace Bootstrap registration in State.md.
	- Do NOT create SDD artifacts such as specify.md, design.md, tasks.md, or verification.md.
	- Do NOT produce numbered implementation lists ( TASK-*, VP-*, DF-*). Classify candidate work types only.
	- Do NOT self-certify verification gates. Identify expectations only; Verifier owns final gate selection.
	- Do NOT paste long chat history as durable truth.
	- Output is a handoff input for research.md Part 1 when persisted by the user.
	### Output Language
	If the user will save output to Documentation/SDD/<feature-slug>/research.md, write all deliverables in English.
